	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"&6&lAdvanced Generators.&r Every other power mod hands you a machine. This one hands you parts."
				""
				"&7You assemble a hollow multiblock from frames and modules - a controller, a fuel input, a heat source, a turbine, an output - and the mod derives the machine's stats from whatever you built. Want more power? Build a bigger box.&r"
				""
				"&e&lIt runs on almost anything&r - solid fuel, liquid fuel or gas - which makes it the natural home for whatever by-product you happen to have too much of."
				""
				"&8Cheap materials, high ceiling, and no tier ladder to grind."
			]
			icon: "advgenerators:controller"
			id: "7E00000000000001"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E01000000000001"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Design the machine yourself"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E02000000000001"
				title: "Begin"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&6Advanced Generators"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 0.8d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E00000000000001"]
			description: [
				"Panels get you started. &eAdvanced Generators&r is what you build when \"more panels\" stops being an answer."
				""
				"It is a multiblock kit rather than a machine: assemble a frame from &eIron Frames&r and &eTubing&r, add a &eController&r, then bolt on the pieces you actually need - fuel tanks, item and fluid inputs, power outputs, heat exchangers, turbine rotors."
				""
				"You design the generator's shape and capacity yourself, which means it scales to whatever your base is actually drawing rather than to a fixed tier."
			]
			icon: "advgenerators:controller"
			id: "7E30300000000002"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "7E30300000000102"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 60
				}
				{
					id: "7E30300000000103"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "&7Build the generator you need"
			tasks: [
				{
					count: 8L
					id: "7E30300000000202"
					item: "advgenerators:iron_frame"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7E30300000000212"
					item: "advgenerators:controller"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7E30300000000222"
					item: "advgenerators:fe_output"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&9Advanced Generators"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E30300000000002"]
			description: [
				"&eAdvanced Generators&r builds generators as multiblocks you design yourself, and the &7Controller&r is the block that makes a pile of parts into a machine."
				""
				"&e&lThe idea:&r you assemble a hollow box from generator modules - a controller, power output, fuel input, and as many capacity modules as you want - and the mod works out its stats from what you built. A bigger box makes more power."
				""
				"&7Right-click the controller to see the assembled machine's rating and whether it is missing anything. It tells you what is wrong rather than silently failing.&r"
				""
				"&8This is the most build-it-yourself power mod in the pack. If you like designing machines rather than placing them, this is your chapter."
			]
			icon: "advgenerators:controller"
			id: "7E00000000000002"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E01000000000002"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Every generator starts here"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E02000000000200"
				item: "advgenerators:controller"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6The Controller"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E00000000000002"]
			description: [
				"&eIron Frames&r, &eTubing&r and &eWiring&r are the structural blocks every Advanced Generators multiblock is built from."
				""
				"&e&lThey are deliberately cheap.&r The cost of a big generator here is bulk iron, not exotic materials - which suits a pack where you are sieving iron by the stack anyway."
				""
				"&7Build the shell first, then fit modules. An incomplete shell will not form, and the controller will tell you which face is open.&r"
			]
			icon: "advgenerators:iron_frame"
			id: "7E00000000000003"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E01000000000003"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7The shell"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7E02000000000300"
					item: "advgenerators:iron_frame"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7E02000000000301"
					item: "advgenerators:iron_tubing"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&6Frames & Tubing"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E00000000000003"]
			description: [
				"A &eHeating Chamber&r burns fuel to make heat; a &eFuel Tank&r buffers what it burns."
				""
				"&e&lWhat you can feed it:&r solid fuel, liquid fuel, or gas. That flexibility is the reason to build one - it will happily run on whatever you have surplus of, which changes as the pack progresses."
				""
				"&7Bio fuel from your Mekanism Crusher, ethene from the PRC, or plain charcoal from surplus saplings all work. Pipe it in and buffer it - a generator fed directly from production stalls whenever production hiccups.&r"
			]
			icon: "advgenerators:heating_chamber"
			id: "7E00000000000004"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E01000000000004"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Feeding the machine"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7E02000000000400"
					item: "advgenerators:heating_chamber"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7E02000000000401"
					item: "advgenerators:fuel_tank"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&6Fuel & Heat"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E00000000000004"]
			description: [
				"A &eSteam Turbine&r converts heat and water into rotational power and then FE; a &eHeat Exchanger&r moves heat between parts of the system."
				""
				"&e&lTurbine kits and rotors come in five tiers&r, and the tier sets both throughput and efficiency. As with Mekanism's Industrial Turbine, the usual bottleneck is not the rotor but everything around it - check the controller readout rather than guessing."
				""
				"&7There is also a Fuel Turbine that burns fuel directly, skipping the steam stage. Less efficient, far simpler, and a reasonable first build.&r"
			]
			icon: "advgenerators:steam_turbine_controller"
			id: "7E00000000000005"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E01000000000005"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Heat into power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E02000000000500"
				item: "advgenerators:steam_turbine_controller"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&6Turbines & Exchangers"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E00000000000004"]
			description: [
				"An &eFE Output&r module is how power leaves the multiblock, and &ePower Capacitors&r buffer it inside."
				""
				"&c&lA generator with no output module produces nothing you can use.&r It will happily run, fill its internal buffer and stop. This is the single most common Advanced Generators mistake."
				""
				"&e&lCapacitor tiers raise internal storage&r, which smooths delivery to a spiky load - the same reasoning as a Mekanism Energy Cube, built into the machine."
				""
				"&7Efficiency Upgrades reduce fuel consumption per FE. On a fuel-limited setup they pay for themselves quickly.&r"
			]
			icon: "advgenerators:fe_output"
			id: "7E00000000000006"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E01000000000006"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
